A47 — resolve the mode by size when no mode carries the requested refresh

`init_drm` hands `-r`, when the launcher gives one, to `preferred_refresh`, and
the mode search requires `mode->vrefresh` to equal it. A connector whose one mode
carries the display's real rate would then yield no output at all for any other
preferred refresh.

The lookup now re-finds by the requested size with the refresh unconstrained, so
a preferred refresh the connector does not advertise still resolves the mode, and
the launch line stays free to pass one.

This is the second half of the old A34, kept when A34's fps cap was parked: the
cap no longer exists, and the size-based lookup stays as insurance.

--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -1385,6 +1385,15 @@
 		mode = find_mode(best->GetModeConnector(), drm->preferred_width, drm->preferred_height, gamescope::ConvertmHzToHz( drm->preferred_refresh ));
 	}
 
+	// gamenative A47: the mode is the display's rate and the connector
+	// advertises only that, so a preferred refresh it does not carry would find
+	// no mode at all. Re-find by size alone rather than let the preference pick
+	// the mode, so the launch line stays free to pass one.
+	if (!mode && drm->preferred_refresh != 0)
+	{
+		mode = find_mode(best->GetModeConnector(), drm->preferred_width, drm->preferred_height, 0);
+	}
+
 	if (!mode && best->GetScreenType() == gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_EXTERNAL) {
 		saved_mode mode_info{};
 		if (get_saved_mode(description, mode_info))
